    "globalConstraints": "- The worker, the clone/capture layer, the entry, the launcher, the four other role files and the kernel are byte-identical to BASE: this plan changes when a reviewer is dispatched, what two role files say, and one cell of the card \u2014 never how a worker runs, how a patch is captured or how a fold merges.\n- The switch defaults off and only ever removes a dispatch: with `reviewOnStateExams: true` in the run's arguments every task gets the one reviewer it gets at BASE and every prompt the run captures is byte-identical to BASE's for the same run; with it off, a task whose record holds a `killed: false`, a stem with no `mutant.json`, or no record at all is reviewed exactly as at BASE.\n- A skipped reviewer never changes what gates a merge: the skip applies only to a task whose pre-review pass left every `Run:`, the exam and every non-minor `Check:` green, and the wave's fold, the candidate suite, the integrated `Run:`/`Check:` passes and the pre-merge gate run on that task exactly as they do on a reviewed one.\n- No shouted imperatives in a role file: the deletions leave `fleet/roles/examiner.md` and `fleet/roles/reviewer.md` in the register they have at BASE, and add no sentence.",
